{"body":{"from":[{"$ref":"1M7360TVPDXC11D"}],"opens":"In order, each step grounding the next. First, the address and the search said in the one language: a place as a route of names in the path, a way of looking as an expression, the old syntax of titles retired, and a route that may begin at a store, as a type named the same in two stores asks; so the reader says where one is by the same functions. Second, patterns, each store's integration answering a pattern's clauses, glass's from an index of arrays, grounded by what ask is actually asked; expressions stay calls. Third, glass's store ships its index, and the lexicon becomes a function. Beside them, as wanted: the statistics and functions the main store declared in an older form said again in the language; the strings nested in records measured. Pinned: time and at, streams, programs. The next session begins at the first step, its bootstrap read through ask.","restsOn":["The plan from here","A store answers patterns","An expression drawn as itself"],"stands":"noted"},"id":"1M7360TVPDXC13W","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000007"],"name":"The plan from here"}
{"body":{"from":[{"$ref":"1M7360TVPDXC11D"}],"opens":"Beside the template, expressions written as TypeScript itself: functions named as the field names them, and a lambda traced by calling it with a stand-in whose keys are reads, so `m => eq(m.value, 3)` becomes the same data. Checked by the compiler and completed by the editor, at the cost of a second face to keep in step with the first.","restsOn":["Expressions are calls, functions give three ways"],"stands":"noted"},"id":"1M7360TVPDXC13X","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000007"],"name":"A face in TypeScript's own syntax"}
{"body":{"from":[{"$ref":"1M7360TVPDXC0V6"}],"opens":"In the language a function named alone is the function itself, given to another as in map(xs, text), and is called only with parentheses or after a pipe; so size(everything) is one, the function, not the field. Kept for now, as the one rule that lets functions be values; whether a function that takes nothing should be called when named alone is open.","restsOn":["Expressions are calls, functions give three ways"],"stands":"noted"},"id":"1M7360TVPDXC13Y","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000007"],"name":"A function named alone"}